Z||000000||Gold-86SE||05-31-2000||10:00 AM||||<BR>Guys, just last evening finished my first transaction with someone from the forum.  Hats off to 80's Boy. What a cool guy.<P>He and I both live in south Tejas and hooked up out on interstate 10 so I could procure my sunroof assembly.<P>Had a great ride to and fro, doing 78/79 most of the way and no traffic of any consequence.<P>80's Boy was great to deal with, and we even swapped couple of tips and tricks.  Hard to meet another Fiero fan and not talk about the cars.<P>On a side note, just as 80's Boy was pulling up another pickup pulled up next to my Gold 86 and asked me "how much?"  So I received my first buy offer last night, but I had to politely(sp) turn down the offer.  Yet, this lead us into a short conversation about the cars and this gentleman owns an 88, and said its been in the family since 88.  Lastly, I just could not pass up the opportunity to tell him about this forum and the great amount of knowledge being passed back and forth here at PFF.<P>Thank you Cliff, we're not worthy, we're not worthy - in the spirit of Wayne and Garth.<BR>||||reg||6
